      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's understandable to feel hesitant, but if you notice anything worsening or if he develops new symptoms, it's important to seek care. You can give your child over-the-counter children's fever reducers like acetaminophen or ibuprofen, if you have parental guidance for dosage, and ensure he stays hydrated. However, it might still be wise to contact your pediatrician to get their input and rule out anything serious.\n\n[Always check product labels and dosage instructions, as some medications are not recommended for children under 3 years old.]",
      "source": "target",
